# Third-Party Notices

This file lists third-party software that may be incorporated into builds of
MediaKit Foundation Framework (MKFF).

## libhevc (Ittiam Systems)

- Project: https://github.com/ittiam-systems/libhevc
- License: Apache License 2.0
- Used when CMake option `MKFF_ENABLE_HEVC_SOFTWARE` is ON (default), or when
  the Cargo feature `hevc-software-fallback` is enabled.
- MKFF fetches a pinned commit via CMake `FetchContent` (or uses a local
  `third_party/libhevc/` tree if present) and links the decoder-only library
  into the core `MKFF` library as an in-process software HEVC fallback.
- Encoder, examples, fuzzers, and upstream unit-test targets are not built
  into MKFF.
- The pinned libhevc decoder supports 8-bit Main (NV12). Main10 / 10-bit
  streams are rejected at the MKFF software wrapper and handled by platform
  hardware decoders instead.

Apache License 2.0 text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Copyright notices and the full Apache-2.0 license text are included in the
upstream libhevc source tree (`LICENSE` / related notice files) fetched at
configure time.

